    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salisbury-University/Purchasing-Manager_JR102152": {
      "title": "Purchasing Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102152 Purchasing Manager (Open) Department: Financial Services - Procurement, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 09-02-2026 Close Date: $72,000 - $75,000 Job Description: Job Summary This position exists to strengthen the University's procurement function by shifting resources from transactional purchasing to strategic sourcing and contract management. The position independently manages complex procurement activities, including formal competitive solicitations, higher-value procurement transactions, contract administration and procurement consulting for campus departments. By analyzing institutional spending, establishing strategic contracts, providing expert procurement guidance and identifying opportunities for continuous improvement, this position will help maximize purchasing value, improve operational efficiency, ensure regulatory compliance and support the University's long-term procurement objectives.  This position has the authority to make procurement decisions and commit the University to puchase goods and services that exceed the standard established threshold set by the University.   Authority and Accountability Reports to Assistant Director of Procurement.  This position will supervise two Buyers and one Buyers Clerk.  This position is not responsible for developing or managing a departmental budget.  Exercises delegated procurement authority to independently manage assigned procurement activities within established purchasing thresholds. Authorized to conduct competitive procurement processes, issue purchase orders, administer contracts, and commit University funds through authorized procurement transactions in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and University policies.  Required/Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in business or related field.   Related experience in which one has gained the knowledge, skills and abilities required for full performance of the work may be substituted for the education requirement on a year for year basis with one year of experience being equivalent to 30 college credits.  Five years of progressively responsible procurement experience  Experience conducting formal competitive procurements Experience supervising, training or providing formal work direction to procurement staff. Preferred Qualifications Public sector procurement experience Professional certification such as CMPA, CPSM, C.P.M., CPPB, CPPO Additional Job Information: The position is a full-time, exempt state role with comprehensive benefits. Priority will be given to applicants who apply by September 16, 2026. However, the position will remain open until filled. Please note, only applications submitted through Salisbury University’s Online Employment Application System will be considered. Any supporting documents must be uploaded with the online application, as documents sent via email will not be accepted. Additionally, three professional references will be required during the final stages of the hiring process. Candidates will be notified prior to their references being contacted. Salisbury University (SU) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. SU is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions."
