    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salisbury-University/Food-Service-Assistant--Part-Time-_JR101724": {
      "title": "Food Service Assistant (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR101724 Food Service Assistant (Part-Time) (Evergreen) (Open) Department: University Dining Svcs-AVP's Office, PM Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Open Date: 03-09-2026 Close Date: $15.00 - $15.75 Job Description: Under direct supervision, provides routine assistance in the preparation and serving of food, sanitation, and/or kitchen maintenance. The Dining Services Department at Salisbury University is accepting applications for  Food Service Assistant (Part-Time Contingent I)  positions in Dining Services in an effort to maintain a pool of applicants for future openings. Once you have applied, if you are selected for an interview, you will be contacted. Primary Job Duties:   Provide routine assistance in the preparation and serving of food; set up and break down service lines; cashiering; maintain safe and sanitary conditions; operate and maintain kitchen equipment such as grills, fryers, ovens, mixers, toasters, etc.; consistently demonstrates excellent customer service skills to all internal and external customers and other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications:   Serve Safe or Food Handler and/or Sanitation Certification required by the end of the first contract period/semester.  Ability to assist in preparing and serving food; to read and write; to perform basic arithmetic computations; to operate food service equipment and appliances; to use kitchen utensils; to work in irritating environments and adverse temperature conditions; to follow oral and written instructions; to lift, transport and stock food service supplies, materials and equipment.  Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs.  Preferred Qualifications:  One year food service experience; High School Diploma or equivalent. Additional Job Information: These are part-time (19 hour) non-exempt contingent positions with no benefits. Salary is up to $15.75 per hour. Working periods include late-August through mid-December and late-January through late-May; work schedules within these periods will vary based upon the needs of the University. Applications will be accepted via Salisbury University's Online Employment Application System. Please visit our website  www.salisbury.edu/hr/careers/  to apply online. See the FAQs of the Online Employment Application System for more information and instructions.  To be considered an applicant, you must apply online and submit the following: Three (3) professional references and complete work history. A cover letter and resume are preferred.  Applications will be reviewed upon receipt. Salisbury University (SU) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. SU is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salisbury-University/Event-Banquet-Server--Part-Time-_JR101722": {
      "title": "Event Banquet Server (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR101722 Event Banquet Server (Part-Time) (Evergreen) (Open) Department: University Dining Svcs-AVP's Office, PM Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Open Date: 03-09-2026 Close Date: $15.00 - $15.75 Job Description: Under direct supervision, provides routine assistance in the preparation and serving of food, sanitation, and/or kitchen maintenance. The Dining Services Department at Salisbury University is accepting applications for   As-Needed Event Banquet Server (Part-Time Contingent I)   positions in Dining Services for current and future openings. Primary Job Duties:   Provide assistance in the set- up, execution and breakdown of various catered events; providing timely service while fulfilling catering requests and maintaining facilities in a high-quality fashion; may on occasions serve alcohol; maintain safe and sanitary conditions; provide different levels of service, constantly demonstrate excellent customer service skills to all customers and other duties as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications:   Must be able to attain ServSafe Safe Food Handlers Certificate no later than the end of the first contract period and TIPS Certification required no later than the second contract period.  Must be able to communicate effectively including reading, writing and verbally; follow instructions; and lift, transport and stock food and food service supplies, material and equipment.  Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs. and be able to work outside as required. Must be well organized, flexible, and a strong team player with the ability to multi-task, adapt to change and provide excellent customer service with or without detailed instructions. Preferred Qualifications:    Restaurant or banquet service experience and High School Diploma or equivalent preferred. Additional Job Information: These are part-time (19 hour) non-exempt contingent positions with no benefits. The starting pay is up to $15.75 per hour.  Catering events occur year-round; work schedules will vary based upon the needs of the University and may include daytime, evening and weekend hours.  To be considered an applicant, you must apply online and submit the following: Three (3) professional references and complete work history. A cover letter and resume are preferred. Applications will be reviewed upon receipt.  Once you have applied, if you are selected for an interview, you will be contacted. Salisbury University (SU) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. SU is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Housekeeper-Assistant--Part-Time-_JR100793": {
      "title": "Housekeeper Assistant (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR100793 Housekeeper Assistant (Part-Time) (Evergreen) Department: Physical Plant-Custodial Services, JM Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Open Date: 01-29-2025 Close Date: Job Description: Under direct supervision, maintains building interiors, ensuring cleanliness, orderliness and attractive conditions are maintained in assigned areas according to set tasks and frequencies. May be required to move furniture and equipment. Salisbury University is accepting applications for a   Housekeeper Assistant , (Part-time Contingent I), in an effort to maintain a pool of applicants for current and future openings. Minimum Qualifications:   Ability to read, write, and perform arithmetic calculations; to operate assigned tools and housekeeping equipment; to work with chemicals and cleaning solutions; to understand and follow directions; to lift up to 30 lbs. and move furniture, equipment and supplies; to transport refuse; and to wear and work in personal protective equipment. Additional Job Information: These are part-time (19 hour) non-exempt contingent positions with no benefits. Salary is $15.00 per hour. Work schedules will vary based upon the needs of the University and may include daytime, evening and weekend hours. To be considered an applicant, you must apply online and submit a complete work history. A resume is preferred. Applications will be reviewed upon receipt.  Once you have applied, if you are selected for an interview, you will be contacted. Diversity and inclusion are core values of Salisbury University. We strive to create a truly diverse and inclusive environment where the richness of ideas, backgrounds, and perspectives of our community is harnessed to create value for our institution, today and in the future. To this end, the University recruits exceptional and diverse faculty, staff, and students from across Maryland, the United States, and around the world, supporting all members of the University community as they work together to achieve institutional goals and vision. To learn more about the University’s commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive campus, please visit   http://www.salisbury.edu/equity/ . Diversity and inclusion are core values of Salisbury University. We strive to create a truly diverse and inclusive environment where the richness of ideas, backgrounds, and perspectives of our community is harnessed to create value for our institution, today and in the future.  To this end, the University recruits exceptional and diverse faculty, staff, and students from across Maryland, the United States, and around the world, supporting all members of the University community as they work together to achieve institutional goals and vision. To learn more about the University’s commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive campus, please visit   http://www.salisbury.edu/equity/ ."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salisbury-University/Housekeeper_JR100792": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR100792 Housekeeper (Evergreen) Department: Physical Plant-Custodial Services, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 01-29-2025 Close Date: Job Description: Under direct supervision, maintains building interiors, ensuring cleanliness, orderliness and attractive conditions are maintained in assigned areas according to set tasks and frequencies. May be required to move furniture and equipment. This position is expected to report to work in emergency situations such as extreme weather conditions when the campus may be closed. Authority and Accountability This position has no supervisory or budgetary authority or accountability. Required/Minimum Qualifications Ability to read, write and perform arithmetic calculations; to operate assigned tools and housekeeping equipment; to work with chemicals and cleaning solutions; to understand and follow directions; to lift and transport supplies and refuse; to wear and work in personal protective equipment.  Must be able to lift up to 30 lbs., and do the following: walking, stooping, kneeling, climbing, standing, twisting, bending, pushing, pulling, crawling. Preferred Qualifications Two years’ experience with housekeeping equipment and/or duties preferred but not required. Additional Job Information: The position is a full-time, non-exempt state role with comprehensive benefits. Please note, only applications submitted through Salisbury University’s Online Employment Application System will be considered. Any supporting documents must be uploaded with the online application, as documents sent via email will not be accepted. Additionally, three professional references will be required during the final stages of the hiring process. Candidates will be notified prior to their references being contacted. Diversity and inclusion are core values of Salisbury University. We strive to create a truly diverse and inclusive environment where the richness of ideas, backgrounds, and perspectives of our community is harnessed to create value for our institution, today and in the future.  To this end, the University recruits exceptional and diverse faculty, staff, and students from across Maryland, the United States, and around the world, supporting all members of the University community as they work together to achieve institutional goals and vision. To learn more about the University’s commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive campus, please visit   http://www.salisbury.edu/equity/ ."
    }
